<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92635" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοθ-έω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥόθος</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make a rushing noise</i>:
			hence, of a <i>roaring</i> fire, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ῥοθοῦντι κριβάνῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					309
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of any
			confused <i>noise</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῦτα . . ἐρρόθουν
				ἐμοί</span> such <i>clamours they raised</i> against me,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				290
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι . . ἐρρόθουν κακοί</span>
			<i>there was a noise of</i> angry words, ib.<i><span class="en">
				259
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
